  "interpretation": [
    "Batch lanes encrypt independent recipient/session messages. Effective device fanout includes recipient devices and sender sync copies.",
    "Wall includes process startup and bytecode loading; runtime rate uses maximum of all five reported Time values including runtime overhead. Online/preprocessing phases shown from party0. Persistent runtime throughput is unmeasured; amortizing startup cannot remove per-send traffic.",
    "Current circuit already reuses prepared HMAC pads within chain derivation and HKDF expansion.",
    "Bandwidth-only ceilings assume the named outgoing link bandwidth is entirely available for reported sent bytes. They are arithmetic bounds, not WAN measurements; RTT, contention, CPU, TLS/H2, and refresh reduce achievable rate.",
    "VM rounds and runtime communication counters are not directly measured WAN roundtrips. No latency estimate multiplies those counters by RTT.",
    "Measured baseline payload is only17B. Realistic256/1024B circuit costs are separate and have no native timing yet.",
    "TLS session reuse amortizes handshake; TLSAESGCM, private H2 framing, ACK/control handling, new sessions, epoch rollover, refresh and erasure remain additional costs.",
    "Tinier128 and packed scheduling are comparison candidates, with no measured speedup included."
  ]
